The attached image illustrates the enhanced uptake of antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) facilitated by Nano-11 nanoparticles. Confocal microscopy images show that soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) is minimally taken up by BMDCs on its own. However, when AF647-labeled Nano-11 is co-incubated with OVA, both the nanoparticles and the antigen are efficiently phagocytized by the dendritic cells and extensively colocalize within the cells, appearing yellow in the merged images. This demonstrates Nano-11's ability to significantly enhance the intracellular delivery of adsorbed protein antigens to BMDCs, which is crucial for initiating an effective immune response as discussed in the context of vaccine adjuvants.